---
description: Apply Shrapwill's software quality standard to every review, change, and addition
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/quality/software-quality.md` before proposing or editing code.

Detect the stack, backend presence, data access, and existing conventions before review. Count code excluding blanks/comments. Treat thresholds as review triggers, apply declarative/test exemptions, and explain deliberate skips. The previous physical-line scanner is a source of candidates, not the current guideline's verdict. Do not hide complexity by compressing formatting.

Review only the requested scope or current changes; skip generated/vendor/build/lockfile content. Reviews are read-only unless edits are requested. Report detected context and skipped checks, then actionable findings ordered by impact. Check layering, repeated logic, validation, and cognitive load using existing module boundaries.

This is a local desktop application. Server, authentication, and database examples in the template apply only if those systems actually exist; do not add them.

Use `CONTRIBUTING.md` for required checks and `docs/architecture.md` for module boundaries.
